    "description": "The base of every AdaptOrDeity cell: the general mechanisms with no transport proteins. A ~2 um disc of membrane (membrane_potential adaptive: capacitor, disc geometry) around a cytosol (energy_metabolism adaptive: bond-graph glycolysis, maintenance ATPase and glycogen), its Na+/K+ (ion_concentrations SN_soma_Argus2026_v01), Ca2+ (Ca_handling adaptive, fixed buffer) and H+ (H_handling adaptive, buffered, pH and E_H) pools, the passive leaks of a lipid membrane (i_leak_Na, i_leak_Ca, i_leak_H), biosynthesis (RNA and lipids, damage and repair, growth towards a daughter), the ribosomes (lost when their upkeep goes unpaid, rebuilt at de novo cost; protein synthesis builds in proportion to them), protein synthesis (protein_expression adaptive), its regulation by falling ATP, G6P, glucose and pH (expression_regulation: every pool's target, growth, and the maintenance: protein synthesis, RNA and lipid upkeep, repair and the maintenance ATPase, each switched on by the game, all off by default) and two protein_pools every cell has: the proteome (ribosomal, nucleoid and other unmodelled proteins) and the glycolytic enzymes (scaling V_gly). Its default values are the fermenter cell's, so a cell type that adds its proteins starts calibrated; alone it has no carriers or pumps, so it runs down (its glucose is spent and its gradients leak away). Cell types extend it: fermenter (generic_adaptive_cell fermenter); later bases add the proteins a class shares (an animal cell: the Na+/K+-ATPase, NCX, ...).",
